    <p>
      I'm a technical leader with 20 years in new-product development, moving
      deliberately from hands-on engineering into project and product leadership.
      I've led cross-functional delivery across three vehicle programs at an EV
      manufacturer, managed an R&amp;D team and third-party development studios in
      regulated casino gaming, and served as Project Manager, Development Lead,
      and Site Manager on a federal simulation contract.
    </p>
    <p>
      I run work the same way across every engagement: discovery first,
      requirements refined with stakeholders, phased plans with
      explicit acceptance criteria and review gates, and plain-spoken schedule
      and risk conversations — owning scope, schedule, and outcomes.
    </p>
    <p>
      I use AI tools as accelerators under human review: tests, diffs, documentation,
      and exploration—not as a substitute for correctness, security, or design judgment.
    </p>
    <p>
      A career spent building demanding real-time software keeps me credible with
      the teams I lead. Currently pursuing PMP certification.
    </p>
